  "method": {
    "images": "Use the pre and post window median images indexed by the individual video frames in each source. The earlier hold window independently checks settled-level stability. All 36 pre, post and earlier-hold median PNGs were regenerated pixel for pixel by decoding the recorded videos and taking medians at their archived indices.",
    "surface": "Read two unprinted flanks locally. Nine-pixel-wide strips are centered at the listed horizontal image positions. Smooth the weighted RGB luminance vertically, find the downward transition into persistently dark liquid, then locate the middle of its local contrast change. The right flank can show a second, higher reflection. Requiring the intensity below the edge to reach the dark-liquid floor rejects this reflection. The left flank avoids the printed one-cup numeral.",
    "x_px_left_right": [
      [97, 104, 111, 118],
      [902, 920, 938, 956]
    ],
    "brightness_model": "Use 0.40 R + 0.45 G + 0.15 B and a vertical Gaussian sigma of 1.65 pixels. Select the strongest local upper-minus-lower transition with a dark floor below. The visually identified high, middle and low windows center on rows 288, 371 and 422 on the left, and 230, 311 and 370 on the right, extending 24 pixels each way.",
    "print_calibration": "Red ink locates five left quarter-cup ticks and four right third-cup ticks in each image. Fit each printed tick locally to a straight line on x=230–325 or x=642–780, project to the transparent flank and linearly interpolate the contact between its two local marks. Use 236.5882365 mL/US cup. Each flank value is the median of its four same-x paired differences. The reported central volume averages the two flank estimates.",
    "sensitivity": "The range repeats each matched contrast at 25%, 50% and 75% of the local transition in each flank, with tick projection to the flank or with the print height at the ruler itself. Curvature and extrapolation to clear glass can shift absolute volume. These are sensitivity ranges from shared images. Vessel calibration tolerance and absolute volumetric accuracy are unmeasured.",
    "timing": "Count matching send, full-drive acknowledgement and completion for every individual pulse. The board reports its elapsed time in integer milliseconds. Serial timestamps describe host traffic and have asymmetric latency. No electrical or shaft-motion timing probe was attached. Finite batch time ends with the last gate. A periodically repeated batch includes its final off interval.",
    "band_labels": {
      "H": "higher cup fill",
      "M": "middle cup fill",
      "L": "lower cup fill",
      "order": "The first letter describes the start. The second describes the end. Actual starting heights differ and are reported in pixels."
    }
  },
